RECORDINGS LICENSE — PENDING

The license for audio/video recordings of Vedic recitation is NOT yet written.
It will be a separate, explicit grant negotiated with the reciters themselves,
and it must say the same thing as the consent form each scholar signs.

Until that grant exists:

  - No recording may be committed, distributed, or published from this project.
  - Recording metadata (manifests) may be tracked in git; the recordings
    themselves live in object storage under access control (see README.md
    in this directory).
  - Every recording must carry a consent_ref and lineage. A recording
    without provenance is worth a fraction of one with it — and a recording
    without consent is not ours to use at all.

This placeholder exists so that nobody mistakes the code license (GPL-3.0)
or the content license (CC-BY-SA 4.0) as covering recordings. They do not.
